```go
// RowTarget is one more registry identity a row answers for, with the kinds the
// view can start again on it (nil = all).
type RowTarget struct {
    Target string
    Kinds  []jobs.Kind
}

type RowQuery struct {
    // ... existing fields unchanged ...
    // Extra are further targets of the same row (a template: its scan directory
    // beside its slug). Their jobs and failures are merged with Target's.
    Extra []RowTarget
}
// resolveRow: active = ActiveOn(Target, Kinds) ++ ActiveOn(each Extra), re-sorted
// stable with running items first; failures = FailuresOn(...) merged, newest first
// (the existing sort). No other change.
```

Tests (input → expected), table-driven, reusing the file's fixtures:
- `Extra` nil → `DescribeRow` / `RowState` identical to today for every existing case (the existing tests stay green unchanged).
- main target idle, extra target with a running item → `State Running`, Detail lead is the extra item's kind verb and its `Name()`.
- main queued (sync), extra running (scan) → `Running`, the running item describes the row (running first after the merge).
- main failed (scan, older), extra failed (sync, newer) → `Failed`, the sync failure wins, Tail ends with `· earlier failure: scan (see :jobs)`.
- main running (sync), extra failed (scan) → `Running`, Tail has `· earlier failure: scan (see :jobs)`.
- extra kinds filter: a `KindSync` failure on the extra target declared `{KindScan}` → ignored (`Idle`).
- other context on the extra target → ignored.
- `RowState(q) == DescribeRow(q).State` for every case above.

Done when: green; `go test ./internal/ui/workspaces/ ./internal/ui/security/ ./internal/ui/oci_resources/` still green (callers unaffected).

